I had decided to startscum monks to get starting smoky potion and wish
for a blindfold, but I got a fountain wish on starting room instead.
I was very surprised to get a wish in so few games and even more
surprised in ascending the first monk that had a starting blindfold,
and I'm a bit sad for messing up such a game: on the castle, while
wearing/taking off levitation boots to get over the traps I once hit
'R' by mistake (instead of 'T') and removed the blindfold for an
instant. Since I immediately put back the blindfold and did not gain
any information, I decided to continue, however. If I didn't have to
startscum for wish/blindfold I would probably do it again, though.

Overall, the monk is an easy role for zen (appart from not starting
with blindfold): martial arts removes necessity for early decent
weapon, and the intrinsics are very useful as usual. I decided to go
for neutral for more peaceful monsters and chance of getting
Magicbane (which I didn't get).

After exploring the first 3 levels and getting to XP 6 I returned to
DL1 to hunt for floating eyes and at around turn 3000 I had telepathy.
I could now enter a couple of shops (general and armour), but I didn't
have much money. I decided to go to minetown for the altar, but it was
crossed aligned. However, I got a magic whistle, BoH and a tame little
dog.
Due to a mistake in pet-buc testing, I ended up wearing cursed +0 iron
shoes, so I could not wear the magic boots I had gotten from the
armour shop (later I found it to be speed boots). While trying to
remove curse with fountains, I got another wish (blessed fixed +2
[oMR). Sokoban was BoH, so I didn't have reflection until after
Medusa.

The next main event was a nurse on DL14: got from 80 to 116 HP at
XL12.
On the Quest level, I successfully hunted for a poly trap and used it
to upgrade my pet. With my brand new minotaur, things got a lot
easier, and I returned to minetown to claim the altar at turn ~25000.
At turn ~3000 I got Vorpal blade and Frost brand.

On a maze level between Medusa and the castle I got silver dragon
scales. Armour gives a huge penalty to hit, but I had maxed luck and
+4 gauntlets of dexterity.
At the castle level, a w ate my minotaur, but I didn't need a pet
anymore and the rest of the game was mostly uneventful.
The correct altar was the third one.

I think I will try my luck with other roles, if I keep getting lucky
with starting room wish/blindfold/towel. I expect healer, priest and
ranger to be the most difficult, but priest ability to detect BUC
should provide very useful if I can get survive long enough for an
artifact weapon.

